WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:06.944
Many health programmes already report to their ministry through DHIS2.

2
00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:11.695
Helena connects Meridian's maternal health project to the district system,

3
00:00:11.695 --> 00:00:14.264
so figures don't have to be typed twice.

4
00:00:14.715 --> 00:00:18.521
She adds a DHIS2 connector for the Lumbini project.

5
00:00:18.521 --> 00:00:22.700
Here it points at the public DHIS2 demonstration server.

6
00:00:26.511 --> 00:00:28.803
A DHIS2 username and password.

7
00:00:28.803 --> 00:00:32.698
The password stays hidden, and is stored encrypted.

8
00:00:33.103 --> 00:00:35.580
She saves it, and tests the connection.

9
00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:43.856
Next, which DHIS2 data set to read, and for which health facility.

10
00:00:43.856 --> 00:00:46.819
She picks the reproductive health data set.

11
00:00:47.223 --> 00:00:50.703
And the facility: Ngelehun community health centre.

12
00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:56.852
The data set's elements are listed.

13
00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:58.859
She maps the two she reports on.

14
00:00:58.859 --> 00:01:02.811
Live births go to births attended by a skilled birth attendant.

15
00:01:03.225 --> 00:01:08.584
She tries postnatal first contacts against the postnatal check indicator.

16
00:01:08.584 --> 00:01:14.163
ImpactMEL warns her: DHIS2 sends a count, and the indicator is a percentage.

17
00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:18.356
A count of visits is not a share of mothers, so she cancels.

18
00:01:18.356 --> 00:01:20.239
Only live births are imported.

19
00:01:20.674 --> 00:01:22.511
Now she imports a period.

20
00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:25.401
The data set is monthly in DHIS2.

21
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:29.127
She picks October, the month that has just closed.

22
00:01:29.566 --> 00:01:35.067
Meridian reports quarterly, so October goes into the October to December quarter.

23
00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:40.228
That draft already exists from an earlier import, so nothing is added twice.

24
00:01:40.228 --> 00:01:43.284
The value is the same, so it stays unchanged.

25
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.289
In Review, under Not sent,

26
00:01:45.289 --> 00:01:48.388
the Lumbini births figure for the fourth quarter is

27
00:01:48.388 --> 00:01:50.878
waiting for someone to check and send it.

28
00:01:51.297 --> 00:01:54.164
The connection also works the other way.

29
00:01:54.164 --> 00:01:59.398
Figures that are already approved in ImpactMEL can be sent back to DHIS2.

30
00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:04.562
Meridian's figures are quarterly, so instead of a month she types the quarter,

31
00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:06.079
April to June, and sends.

32
00:02:06.523 --> 00:02:11.621
DHIS2 reports back what it accepted, and the run log keeps the record.

33
00:02:12.043 --> 00:02:16.658
Figures come in from DHIS2 as drafts, get checked like any other,

34
00:02:16.658 --> 00:02:18.717
and approved figures go back.

35
00:02:18.717 --> 00:02:20.705
One record, in both systems.
